      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is for modules with `vendor_ramdisk_available`, not `vendor_ramdisk`, having an rc file makes sense. e.g. for snapuserd:\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/system/core/+/1515001/1/fs_mgr/libsnapshot/Android.bp#b442\n\ncc_binary {\n    name: \"snapuserd\",\n    init_rc: [\n        \"snapuserd.rc\",\n    ],\n    vendor_ramdisk_available: true,\n    // ...\n}\n\nThen, we want the core variant to have the rc file, but the ramdisk / vendor_ramdisk variant to not have it.\n\nI don\u0027t know how to distinguish between vendor_ramdisk and vendor_ramdisk_available in this context, though...",
